# Attachments

An attachment is a file someone opens or downloads, such as a log, a YAML file or a PDF.

<h2 id="wg-085">Offer a usable alternative</h2>

Say what the file is, its format and size. Where a person needs the content, give it as page text too.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Download | Download the heating schedule (PDF, 82KB) |
| See the attached document. | The heating schedule is shown below. You can also download it as a PDF. |

<h2 id="wg-064">Describe formats accurately</h2>

Do not call a transcript a sign language version. Do not show a play button until a reviewed video exists. For example, if help for the room controls exists only as written instructions, show those and say plainly that there is no signed version yet.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Watch the signed video. (no video exists) | A written version is available. A British Sign Language version has not been made yet. |
| BSL transcript | Written transcript. A BSL video has not been made. |

## Logs and diagnostics

Say what the file contains and who can see it. Tell people to check it for private details before sharing.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Send us your logs. | Download diagnostics (.json, 140KB). It contains device names and times. Check it for anything private before you send it. |
